{
  "_comment": [
    ".claude/settings.json — the per-repository settings Claude Code reads.",
    "  cp templates/claude/settings.json.example .claude/settings.json",
    "",
    "This is the Claude Code half of the pair whose Codex half is",
    "templates/codex/config.toml.example. The two files configure the SAME two",
    "things — a date stamp on every turn, and where memory is kept — because",
    "those are the two places where a CLI's own defaults quietly change what",
    "your agent believes. Everything else about this kit is CLI-agnostic on",
    "purpose (see AGENTS.md).",
    "",
    "JSON has no comments, so this key is the comment. Claude Code ignores",
    "unknown keys; leaving it in place costs nothing.",
    "",
    "hooks.UserPromptSubmit: the command's stdout is prepended to your turn.",
    "An agent that guesses today's date writes a deadline on the wrong weekday,",
    "and a wrong '(Mon)' does not look wrong on re-reading — the only way to",
    "catch it is to compare against a clock outside the model. So state it.",
    "",
    "autoMemoryDirectory: where this CLI keeps its own memory. Read AGENTS.md",
    "on what that memory is allowed to be: a CACHE. The single source of truth",
    "is the plain files (ssot/, judgment/, approval_queue.md, verifiers.md,",
    "system_map.md, projects/*/charter.md) and nothing else. Delete the memory",
    "directory and the loop must still be correct — only slower.",
    "Replace <ABSOLUTE-PATH-TO-YOUR-WORK-LOOP> below, or drop the key entirely",
    "to use the CLI's default location."
  ],
  "hooks": {
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "date '+[now] %Y-%m-%d (%a) %H:%M %Z'"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "autoMemoryDirectory": "<ABSOLUTE-PATH-TO-YOUR-WORK-LOOP>/local/memory"
}
